WEBVTT

00:00:00.107 --> 00:00:01.493
Welcome to the course:

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:07.120
Conversational AI concepts, capabilities, and use cases.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:14.800
Think about the last time you interacted with a chat bot at work or as a customer.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.213
Maybe it answered a simple question right away,

00:00:18.213 --> 00:00:25.314
or maybe it sent you through a few fixed options and left you feeling stuck

00:00:25.314 --> 00:00:28.840
when your question did not quite fit.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.520
That difference in experience is not accidental.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.027
It comes down to how the conversational system is designed,

00:00:38.394 --> 00:00:43.680
what it is capable of understanding, and how it is implemented.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:50.687
This course focuses on helping you understand those differences

00:00:50.687 --> 00:00:55.293
so you can evaluate conversational AI solutions with clarity

00:00:55.293 --> 00:00:58.400
and make better decisions in a business context.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.587
By the end of this course, you will be able to explain what

00:01:02.587 --> 00:01:08.225
Conversational AI is and how it differs from traditional automation systems

00:01:08.225 --> 00:01:12.160
such as IVR and rule based chat bots.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:18.193
Describe how Conversational AI works, including the key technologies

00:01:18.193 --> 00:01:23.893
that enable it to understand input, interpret intent, and generate responses,

00:01:23.893 --> 00:01:29.032
and differentiate between traditional chat bots, AI chat bots,

00:01:29.032 --> 00:01:34.293
and a gentic AI chat bots, and evaluate implementation approaches

00:01:34.318 --> 00:01:37.760
based on organizational needs and capabilities.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.120
What is conversational AI and how is it different?

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.777
Before we talk about how conversational AI works or where it is used,

00:01:47.802 --> 00:01:50.040
we need to start with something more basic.

00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:53.807
We need to understand what makes an interaction a true conversation

00:01:53.807 --> 00:01:57.720
and why this kind of AI is different from the systems that came before it.

00:01:58.606 --> 00:02:02.347
Most of us have interacted with some form of automation,

00:02:02.347 --> 00:02:05.600
but not all automated systems are conversational.

00:02:05.886 --> 00:02:11.595
This distinction matters because it shapes how people experience technology

00:02:11.595 --> 00:02:12.560
in real life.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.840
Let us begin with a simple scenario.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.000
Meet Emily.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.520
Emily needs help with a recent bank transaction.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.040
She calls customer support and is greeted by an automated system.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:30.004
The voice asks her to press one for account details,

00:02:30.197 --> 00:02:35.280
press 2 for card services, and press 3 for recent transactions.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.560
Emily listens carefully, presses a number, and waits.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.800
A new menu begins to play.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.720
She presses another option and waits again.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.493
After a few more steps, she realizes the option she needs is not

00:02:49.493 --> 00:02:50.560
listed at all.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.880
She hangs up, slightly frustrated, without any solution.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.707
Later that day, Emily opens the bank's website and

00:02:58.707 --> 00:03:00.600
starts a chat instead.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.720
This time she types I need help with a transaction that looks wrong.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.800
The system responds with a follow up question and asks for more details.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.093
The conversation continues step by step

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:17.120
until Emily gets the information she needs.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.588
Both interactions involved automation,

00:03:20.588 --> 00:03:23.840
but only one of them felt like a conversation.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:29.560
This difference helps us understand what conversational AI really is.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:34.993
Conversational AI refers to systems that can engage in dialogue with users

00:03:34.993 --> 00:03:37.120
in an organic and flexible way.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.292
These interactions can take place through written text, voice conversations,

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.560
or web based chat interfaces.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:49.287
Unlike older systems, conversational AI is not limited

00:03:49.287 --> 00:03:52.360
to rigid menus or predefined paths.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.807
It is designed to understand what users are trying to communicate,

00:03:56.807 --> 00:04:00.160
even when the wording is informal or imperfect.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.887
As a result, interactions feel more responsive

00:04:03.887 --> 00:04:04.960
and more human.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:11.299
Traditional systems such as IVR or interactive Voice response,

00:04:11.486 --> 00:04:13.600
were built around fixed options.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.313
They work well for simple, predictable requests,

00:04:17.313 --> 00:04:22.293
but struggle when users need to explain context or ask questions

00:04:22.293 --> 00:04:23.799
in unexpected ways.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:30.440
Once a user steps outside the predefined flow, these systems cannot easily adapt.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.680
Conversational AI allows users to speak or type naturally.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.320
The system interprets intent and responds in a way that keeps the interaction

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.320
moving forward.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:48.640
Instead of forcing users to follow rigid steps, the technology adapts to them.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:55.280
This is what separates basic automation from true conversational experiences.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:03.760
One of the earliest examples was Eliza, created in 1964 by Joseph Weizenbaum.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:09.298
Eliza simulated conversation by matching patterns in user input,

00:05:09.491 --> 00:05:14.560
creating the illusion of understanding even though it followed simple rules.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.504
Later, Alice, developed by Richard Wallace,

00:05:18.572 --> 00:05:23.416
expanded on this approach using structured pattern matching and scripted

00:05:23.416 --> 00:05:24.199
responses.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.993
Cleverbot took another step forward by learning from past conversations with

00:05:29.018 --> 00:05:32.491
real users, allowing it to generate more varied

00:05:32.491 --> 00:05:35.080
and less predictable replies.

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:40.216
Modern assistance such as Siri, Google Assistant,

00:05:40.241 --> 00:05:43.960
and Cortana represent a major leap forward.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:50.016
Advances in language processing and computing power now allow these systems

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:54.323
to understand context, manage longer conversations,

00:05:54.323 --> 00:05:57.080
and respond more accurately over time.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.793
Today, conversational AI plays a real role in

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:05.280
in how customers find information, get support, and interact with businesses.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.998
Understanding how it differs from older systems sets the foundation for

00:06:09.998 --> 00:06:11.840
everything else in this course.

00:06:12.706 --> 00:06:16.911
In the next section, we will explore how conversational AI

00:06:16.911 --> 00:06:18.600
works behind the scenes.

00:06:19.793 --> 00:06:22.106
How Conversational AI Works.

00:06:22.106 --> 00:06:25.073
With a clear understanding of what conversational AI

00:06:25.097 --> 00:06:27.996
is, the next logical question that follows

00:06:28.021 --> 00:06:29.600
is how it actually works.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.889
While interacting with conversational AI can feel simple,

00:06:33.889 --> 00:06:36.320
a lot is happening behind the scenes.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:41.384
Each message goes through a series of steps that work together to capture input,

00:06:41.622 --> 00:06:45.560
understand meaning, and generate an appropriate response.

00:06:45.695 --> 00:06:49.942
These steps happen in real time and are designed to make interactions

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.960
feel natural and efficient.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:57.200
At a high level, conversational AI follows a clear process.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:03.800
It begins by capturing the user's input, whether that input is text or voice.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:09.333
Voice interactions rely on ASR or automatic speech recognition,

00:07:09.599 --> 00:07:13.800
which converts spoken language into text the system can process.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:18.020
Next, the system analyzes the language itself

00:07:18.045 --> 00:07:21.560
using NLP, or natural language processing.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:26.176
This helps break the input into structured components that can be

00:07:26.176 --> 00:07:27.880
interpreted more accurately.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:34.469
Once the language is processed, NLU or Natural Language Understanding

00:07:34.469 --> 00:07:35.720
comes into play.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:39.976
This is where the system determines intent and context,

00:07:39.976 --> 00:07:45.960
focusing on what the user is trying to achieve rather than the exact words used.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:51.760
With intent understood, the system decides how to respond.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:55.400
It may retrieve information, generate a reply,

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:59.040
or ask a follow up question to move the interaction forward.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:04.011
Finally, conversational AI systems improve over

00:08:04.036 --> 00:08:06.760
time by learning from interactions.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:14.185
Feedback, usage patterns, and outcomes help refine future responses

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.440
and make conversations more effective.

00:08:17.135 --> 00:08:22.228
Modern conversational AI also benefits from enhancements such as

00:08:22.228 --> 00:08:27.624
speech synthesis, retrieval, augmented generation, vector databases,

00:08:27.624 --> 00:08:29.639
and real time translation.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:36.320
These technologies further improve accuracy, responsiveness, and scalability.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:39.521
Together, these components explain how

00:08:39.546 --> 00:08:45.360
conversational AI moves from a simple input to a meaningful response.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:48.807
In the next section, we will explore how these capabilities

00:08:48.807 --> 00:08:52.100
appear in different types of conversational AI systems

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.359
used in practice.

00:08:58.675 --> 00:09:01.787
Conversational AI in Practice.

00:09:01.787 --> 00:09:05.740
So far, we have explored what conversational

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:09.480
AI is and how it works behind the scenes.

00:09:10.415 --> 00:09:15.420
The next step is understanding how these capabilities are applied in real

00:09:15.445 --> 00:09:16.600
organizations.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:21.628
In practice, not all conversational AI systems are

00:09:21.653 --> 00:09:22.665
built the same.

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:27.182
They differ in how much they can understand, how flexible they are,

00:09:27.182 --> 00:09:30.120
and how much responsibility they can take on.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:34.500
These differences matter because choosing the right type of system

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:39.160
has a direct impact on cost, risk, and business outcomes.

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:44.131
To make sense of this, conversational AI can be grouped into 3

00:09:44.131 --> 00:09:52.280
broad categories, Traditional chat bots, AI chat bots, and a gentic AI chat bots.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:56.800
Traditional chat bots are the simplest form of conversational systems.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:01.080
They rely on predefined rules and keyword based logic.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:06.640
Conversations follow scripted paths, often built using decision trees.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:12.437
A user asks a question and the chat bot matches it to a known pattern before

00:10:12.437 --> 00:10:14.400
delivering a fixed response.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:19.382
Because of this design, traditional chat bots are usually limited

00:10:19.407 --> 00:10:21.360
to single turn interactions.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:28.303
They work best for predictable and repetitive tasks such as FAQs or basic

00:10:28.328 --> 00:10:29.665
information requests.

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:33.080
However, they struggle when users phrase questions

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:36.320
differently or need to provide additional context.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:42.208
AI Chat bots use language models to understand nuance, synonyms,

00:10:42.233 --> 00:10:43.560
and varied phrasing.

00:10:43.655 --> 00:10:46.100
Instead of relying on rigid scripts,

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:49.493
they generate responses dynamically based on intent

00:10:49.493 --> 00:10:50.680
and context.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:57.068
Conversations can span multiple turns, allowing users to ask follow up questions

00:10:57.068 --> 00:10:58.880
or refine their requests.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:02.287
Naturally, AI chat bots are well suited for handling

00:11:02.287 --> 00:11:06.440
a broader range of simple to moderately complex interactions.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:09.687
Over time, they also improve by learning from

00:11:09.687 --> 00:11:12.560
conversation patterns and user feedback.

00:11:13.006 --> 00:11:18.417
Agentic AI chat bots are advanced systems that go beyond understanding and

00:11:18.417 --> 00:11:19.200
responding.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.440
They are designed to take action.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:27.207
Agentic AI chat bots can use additional inputs such as conversation history,

00:11:27.207 --> 00:11:30.520
user context, or uploaded information.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.000
They can trigger workflows, make decisions,

00:11:34.025 --> 00:11:36.920
and complete tasks from start to finish.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:42.240
Instead of stopping at an answer, these systems focus on outcomes.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:47.580
They adapt their behavior based on results and learn from the actions they

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:50.907
take, allowing them to operate with a higher

00:11:50.907 --> 00:11:52.200
level of autonomy.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:56.087
Understanding the different types of conversational AI

00:11:56.087 --> 00:12:01.120
is only part of the picture in real organizations.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:06.320
The next challenge is deciding how to implement these systems effectively.

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:11.580
Some organizations choose to build conversational AI systems

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.720
entirely on their own.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:18.080
This approach offers maximum control and customization,

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:23.495
but it also requires strong engineering capability, ongoing maintenance,

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:25.080
and long term investment.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:31.593
It is best suited for organizations with a proven track record of building complex

00:12:31.593 --> 00:12:32.920
internal platforms.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:39.093
Another approach is to build solutions using frameworks provided by large cloud

00:12:39.118 --> 00:12:40.080
platforms.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:45.059
This reduces development effort and integrates more easily with existing

00:12:45.084 --> 00:12:46.400
enterprise systems.

00:12:46.613 --> 00:12:49.433
However, it also creates dependency on a specific

00:12:49.433 --> 00:12:53.385
technology stack and still requires specialized skills to customize and

00:12:53.385 --> 00:12:54.480
support the solution.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.489
Alternatively, many organizations choose to work with

00:12:58.489 --> 00:13:01.000
conversational AI specialists.

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:07.120
This approach accelerates deployment and reduces the need for in house expertise.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:11.320
In some cases, industry specific models

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:13.680
can further reduce time and cost.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:17.620
The trade off is reduced control over the solution.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:22.360
There is no single right approach to conversational AI.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:28.960
The most successful implementations align with how an organization already works.

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:32.219
Companies that thrive on internal development

00:13:32.219 --> 00:13:34.920
may succeed by building in house.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:38.800
Others perform better by partnering with specialists.

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:44.498
For corporate teams, the real value lies in understanding the options,

00:13:44.498 --> 00:13:49.250
recognizing trade offs, and choosing an approach that fits their

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:52.800
organization's capabilities and business goals.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:57.547
Congratulations, you have successfully completed the

00:13:57.547 --> 00:14:03.400
course Conversational AI: Concepts, Capabilities, and Use Cases.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:07.994
In this course, you learned that conversational AI

00:14:07.994 --> 00:14:12.401
enables more natural, flexible interactions than traditional

00:14:12.401 --> 00:14:18.400
automation by understanding intent, context, and varied user input.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:23.588
Conversational AI works through a series of coordinated steps,

00:14:23.588 --> 00:14:29.059
including input capture, language processing, intent understanding,

00:14:29.059 --> 00:14:32.760
response generation, and continuous learning.

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:38.112
And different types of conversational AI systems serve different business needs,

00:14:38.225 --> 00:14:43.165
and choosing the right approach requires balancing capabilities, risk,

00:14:43.165 --> 00:14:45.120
and organizational readiness.